    "requestChance": 0.35,
    "middleVsGreat": 0.3,
    "pettyVsGreat": 0.15
  },
  "suzerainty": {
    "note": "M29 B: how petty kings become vassals. Protection: a petty king truly threatened (at war, or an army mustering against it) at danger dangerAbove or more asks, at chance a month, the great power he likes best (relation plus strengthWeight x log10 of its power, less distanceWeight a map unit and perVassal for each vassal it holds); the crown hears it in the inbox for askDays (refused: relation refuseRelation, no new ask for askAgainDays), an AI power takes him at once. The crown's own offer of protection succeeds at base + dangerWeight x danger + relationWeight x relation (at most most), and may not be repeated for cooldown days. Pressure: base + fearWeight x the realm's fear of Temeria (M19) + giftWeight per giftPer crowns of gift + relationWeight x relation + ratioWeight x log2 of the crown's power over theirs (at most ratioMost), at most most; refused, relation refuseRelation; cooldown days between tries. AI great powers press a petty neighbour within reach whose power is ratio times less and whose affinity is affinity or more, at chance a month. An AI power holds at most most vassals. A new vassal's loyalty by route; its ambition starts at ambition. Mahakam takes protection only.",
    "ambition": 20,
    "protection": { "dangerAbove": 0.6, "chance": 0.3, "loyalty": 60, "askDays": 45, "refuseRelation": -8, "askAgainDays": 365, "strengthWeight": 10, "distanceWeight": 0.03, "perVassal": 15 },
    "offer": { "base": 0.1, "dangerWeight": 0.35, "relationWeight": 0.006, "most": 0.9, "loyalty": 55, "cooldown": 180 },
    "pressure": { "base": -0.35, "fearWeight": 0.012, "giftPer": 500, "giftWeight": 0.08, "relationWeight": 0.004, "ratioWeight": 0.08, "ratioMost": 0.3, "most": 0.9, "loyalty": 25, "refuseRelation": -12, "cooldown": 365, "gifts": [0, 500, 1500] },
    "peace": { "loyalty": 35 },
    "ai": { "reach": 900, "ratio": 3, "affinity": 0, "chance": 0.01, "most": 3 }
  },
  "vassals": {
    "note": "M29 C: vassal kings as lords abroad. Loyalty drifts by loyalty.drift a month toward loyalty.base plus relationWeight x relations with the suzerain (affinity for an AI one), less tributeWeight for each step of tribute demanded above the usual; ambition grows ambitionPerMonth. Tribute is tribute.share of his income times his tribute setting, all of it from loyalty fullAbove, none below noneBelow (Mahakam pays none). Called to arms he sends retinue.share of his kingdom's potential army, all from fullAbove, half below, none under refuseBelow. At loyalty guardAbove he breaks a camp or lair in his lands at guardChance a month. Attacked, he expects his suzerain at war with the attacker within protection.graceDays: answered, loyalty +answered; ignored, loyalty ignored, and every other vassal of that suzerain othersNotice. Below court.below a rival great power may court him (chance a month): the crown is warned first, and after warnDays still disloyal he goes over (loyalty court.loyalty); the crown can outbid the rival (matchCoin, +matchLoyalty) or warn him (+warnLoyalty and his heir at Vizima for warnHostageDays). Below revolt.below with ambition over ambitionAbove and no heir held, he may rise (chance a month) in a war for independence; his capital taken, he comes to the Judgement. Mahakam resents meddling: a summons or a hostage costs mahakamMeddle loyalty.",
    "ambitionPerMonth": 1,
    "loyalty": { "base": 45, "relationWeight": 0.4, "tributeWeight": 30, "drift": 0.05 },
